view","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices are "},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the columns, the hyperedges, are at positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0..<hyperedgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The matrix conforms to "},{"code":"Hypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it unchanged. It is not a "},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", even when built from one, because a cell edit can give a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column any number of bits."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A column is any set of vertices. Empty columns and repeated columns are kept. A graph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop becomes the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the directed form, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" is the sparse representation of the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraphs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Storage","text":"Storage","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both orientations are stored: n rows of ⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row and column popcounts cached. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of ⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual, swaps the two orientations in O(1). The storage is 2·n·m\/8 bytes, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the matrix suits dense or small incidence, such as spectral work or hypergraphs with large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" for sparse incidence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape, so column order counts."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"’s equality ignores positions."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/init(vertexCount:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"init(vertexCount:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A matrix of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" vertices and no columns."}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/init(vertexcount:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertexCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(vertexCount:)"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-4158r":{"role":"symb